 "_about": "the sengoku-bune of the Edo coastal trade (the higaki and taru-kaisen of the Osaka-Edo run, the kitamae-bune of the Sea of Japan): a slab-sided, flat-bottomed hull with a long raked stem, an open transom stern carrying a huge rudder, the cargo walled in amidships by removable side boards, one great square sail of cotton strips on a single mast. (A 1000-koku ship about 29 m overall and 7.5 m in the beam, from the Naniwa-maru reconstruction (Osaka Maritime Museum); the sail about 18 x 20 m)",
